{#
    Webmention endpoint discovery.

    A sending site fetches one of my pages, looks for these, and POSTs the
    notification to whichever it finds. The site is static, so both point at
    webmention.io, which holds the endpoint on its behalf — src/_data/webmentions.js
    pulls what it collects back in at build time.

    The pingback endpoint is webmention.io's bridge for the older protocol, so
    blogs still sending pingbacks are handled without a second service.

    Both URLs are built from metadata.webmention.domain, which must be exactly
    the domain the webmention.io account was created under — the same string
    the API is queried with in src/_data/webmentions.js. See WEBMENTIONS.md.
#}
<link rel="webmention" href="https://webmention.io/{{ metadata.webmention.domain }}/webmention">
<link rel="pingback" href="https://webmention.io/{{ metadata.webmention.domain }}/xmlrpc">
